            "id": "1",
            "text": "**Red\u2011flag:** Possible septicemia in an immunosuppressed renal\u2011transplant patient \u2013 a life\u2011threatening infection that could progress to shock within the hour.\n\n**Stabilising measure:** Obtain two sets of **blood cultures** (aerobic\u202f+\u202fanaerobic) and start empiric broad\u2011spectrum IV antibiotics (e.g., vancomycin\u202f+\u202fcefepime) **after** the cultures are drawn.\n\n**Single test to order first:** **Blood cultures** \u2013 they are the quickest way to identify\u2014or rule out\u2014a bacterial (or fungal) bloodstream infection, which is the most immediate threat in this scenario.  \n\n*Synthetic teaching case - not medical advice.*",
            "response_type": "text"
          }
